Subject: [PATCH] mppdec: HEVC -- the broadcast's own timestamps, in microseconds

Measured on a DVB-S 2160p50 HEVC broadcast (TRT 4K) on RK3588, at every
opening of the channel (2026-10-31): the timestamps MPP makes up for HEVC
(use_mpp_pts) came out as one time for some fifty pictures, and the pictures
behind it were thrown away downstream as not after the one before -- 320 and
360 ms of picture gone in two of three openings. The same fault, and the
same answer, as 0002 for H.264: the broadcast's PTS in microseconds.

---
--- a/gst/rockchipmpp/gstmppdec.c
+++ b/gst/rockchipmpp/gstmppdec.c
@@ -375,7 +375,8 @@ gst_mpp_dec_set_format (GstVideoDecoder * decoder, GstVideoCodecState * state)
   GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (self, "setting format: %" GST_PTR_FORMAT, state->caps);
 
   /* The MPP m2vd's PTS is buggy */
-  if (self->mpp_type == MPP_VIDEO_CodingMPEG2 || self->mpp_type == MPP_VIDEO_CodingAVC) {
+  if (self->mpp_type == MPP_VIDEO_CodingMPEG2 || self->mpp_type == MPP_VIDEO_CodingAVC ||
+      self->mpp_type == MPP_VIDEO_CodingHEVC) {
     self->use_mpp_pts = FALSE;
 
     /* It is not, given the unit it reads: m2vd times each picture from its
@@ -395,7 +396,13 @@ gst_mpp_dec_set_format (GstVideoDecoder * decoder, GstVideoCodecState * state)
      * downstream as not after the one before: 150-480 ms of picture missing
      * at every channel opening. Given the broadcast's own PTS in
      * microseconds, h264d starts at the key frame and times every field
-     * 20 ms apart (measured 2026-10-30 on a recording of that channel). */
+     * 20 ms apart (measured 2026-10-30 on a recording of that channel).
+     *
+     * HEVC as well: the timestamps MPP makes up for h265d came out as one
+     * time for some fifty pictures at the opening of a channel (TRT 4K,
+     * 2160p50, measured 2026-10-31), and the pictures behind them were
+     * thrown away downstream as not after the one before -- a third of a
+     * second of picture gone. */
     self->pts_in_us = TRUE;
   }
 
